  {
   "id": "gd_05",
   "title": "Mo chù: lenition and liking",
   "level": 3,
   "teacher": {
    "zone": "tobermory_mishnish",
    "x": 11,
    "y": 6,
    "name": "Calum",
    "sprite": "poet"
   },
   "intro": [
    "Gaelic softens the start of a word after certain little words. It's called lenition.",
    "You write it with an h after the first letter. Cù, a dog. Mo chù, my dog."
   ],
   "words": [
    {
     "id": "mo_chu",
     "local": "mo chù",
     "english": "my dog",
     "say": "moh CHOO",
     "note": "Cù gains an h after mo, 'my', and the c goes soft, like 'loch'."
    },
    {
     "id": "mo_chat",
     "local": "mo chat",
     "english": "my cat",
     "say": "moh CHAHT"
    },
    {
     "id": "a_chu",
     "local": "a chù",
     "english": "his dog",
     "say": "uh CHOO",
     "note": "His softens the word."
    },
    {
     "id": "a_cu",
     "local": "a cù",
     "english": "her dog",
     "say": "uh KOO",
     "note": "Her doesn't. The only clue to whose dog it is."
    },
    {
     "id": "gle_mhath",
     "local": "glè mhath",
     "english": "very good",
     "say": "glay VAH",
     "note": "Glè, 'very', softens: math becomes mhath."
    },
    {
     "id": "is_toil_leam",
     "local": "Is toil leam...",
     "english": "I like...",
     "say": "iss TOL lum",
     "note": "Is toil leam tì: I like tea."
    },
    {
     "id": "cha_toil_leam",
     "local": "Cha toil leam...",
     "english": "I don't like...",
     "say": "cha TOL lum"
    },
    {
     "id": "cait_a_bheil",
     "local": "Càit a bheil...?",
     "english": "Where is...?",
     "say": "KAATCH uh VAYL"
    },
    {
     "id": "tha_gaidhlig_agam",
     "local": "Tha Gàidhlig agam",
     "english": "I speak Gaelic",
     "say": "HA GAH-lik AH-kum",
     "note": "Word for word: Gaelic is at me. Add 'beagan', a little, to be honest."
    }
   ],
   "tip": "Lenition adds an h: c becomes ch, m becomes mh (said 'v'), b becomes bh (also 'v'). That's why it's madainn mhath, not madainn math."
  },
